      "description": "Abbot Hall - @Abbot Hall, Kirkland, Kendal - 'Abbot Hall. Abbot Hall was built on a medieval site in the fashionable Palladian style between 1759 and 1762 for Colonel and Mrs. George Wilson, reputedly to the design of Carr of York. Planned as a country house in the town, Abbot Hall soon became Kendal's premier residential address. It was threatened with demolition in the 1930s and 1950s but a charitable trust saved the building and now runs it as an award-winning art gallery.' by Kendal Civic Society (openplaques.org ID=11514)",
